  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the vacancy in the vice presidency, President Prabowo Subianto has proposed two candidates, Minister of Agriculture Andi Amran Sulaiman and Sugiono, to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR). The legislative body has initiated a formal verification process, which includes confirming the educational backgrounds and academic diplomas of both candidates. While the proposal has gained significant media attention, Andi Amran Sulaiman has publicly expressed surprise at the nomination, emphasizing that he is prioritizing his ongoing work for Indonesian farmers and infrastructure development, such as irrigation projects. Political figures, including those from the PDIP, have begun providing assessments of the proposed candidates. The selection process is expected to conclude on December 11. Public interest remains high as the administration moves forward with the selection process to fill the role previously held by Gibran.",
